Chapter: WorldCheck
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter ListUtils
  cites Safari chapter Cat
  cites Safari chapter World
  cites Judge chapter Grade
  cites Gold chapter WorldGold

 Grade the World port against wasm/world.zig.

 SEAM 2, AND THE PUREST INSTANCE OF IT HERE. world.zig draws nothing and projects
 nothing: it is authored data plus the deterministic generators that expand it. So
 almost everything is graded EXACTLY -- every count, every colour, every codepoint,
 every flag, every segment's exit target. The only Reals whose width could differ
 are the jitter sines in the herds, the turn angles in radians, and the commit
 point that divides by a tangent, and those take the relative gate.

 EVERYTHING IS DUMPED. Every tree, every cow, every pig, the gaze pig, and the cat
 placement -- not a summary. A data module graded on a summary is a data module
 not graded, and this one is 19 segments of hand-authored schedule where a single
 transposed flag is a different route.

 THE THINGS MOST WORTH GETTING WRONG, and what catches each:

   the pig novelty rule -- only the first TWO pig legs are distraction herds, so
   `w-npigs` reads 49 on segments 3 and 11 and 10 everywhere else pigs appear.
   An off-by-one in the counter changes a 49 to a 10 and the count says so.

   the bull's debut -- absent for four segments, then a staple. `w-ncows` steps
   14 to 15 at segment 5, and `w-cowface` carries the one False among the Trues,
   because the bull faces the other way.

   the terminus -- segment 19 exits to ITSELF, has no creature, and commits at its
   own end rather than short of a turn it does not have.

   the accumulated heading -- each segment's is the previous one plus a signed
   turn, so an error at segment 2 is still there at segment 19. The drift is
   visible in the gold: segment 13's heading is -0.87266487 where segment 1's
   angle is 0.87266463, and that is accumulation, not a typo.

 We say:

Section: The Segments

  segs : List Segment
  segs = build-world

  lengths : List Segment, Integer -> List Real
  lengths (ss) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ss then []
    else [(list-at ss i).length] & lengths ss (i + 1)

  n-trees : List Segment, Integer -> List Integer
  n-trees (ss) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ss then []
    else [list-length (list-at ss i).trees] & n-trees ss (i + 1)

  n-cows : List Segment, Integer -> List Integer
  n-cows (ss) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ss then []
    else [list-length (list-at ss i).cows] & n-cows ss (i + 1)

  n-pigs : List Segment, Integer -> List Integer
  n-pigs (ss) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ss then []
    else [list-length (list-at ss i).pigs] & n-pigs ss (i + 1)

  distracts : List Segment, Integer -> List Boolean
  distracts (ss) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ss then []
    else [(list-at ss i).pigs-distract] & distracts ss (i + 1)

  terminates-of : List Segment, Integer -> List Boolean
  terminates-of (ss) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ss then []
    else [(list-at ss i).terminates] & terminates-of ss (i + 1)

  has-cats : List Segment, Integer -> List Boolean
  has-cats (ss) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ss then []
    else [(list-at ss i).has-cat] & has-cats ss (i + 1)

  mid-towers : List Segment, Integer -> List Boolean
  mid-towers (ss) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ss then []
    else [(list-at ss i).has-mid-tower] & mid-towers ss (i + 1)

  exit-rights : List Segment, Integer -> List Boolean
  exit-rights (ss) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ss then []
    else [(list-at ss i).exit-right] & exit-rights ss (i + 1)

  exit-tos : List Segment, Integer -> List Integer
  exit-tos (ss) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ss then []
    else [(list-at ss i).exit-to] & exit-tos ss (i + 1)

 The probe prints the enum's ordinal, so the port answers in the same order the
 zig declares them: none, elephant, giraffe, zebra, rhino, pond.

  creature-ord : Creature -> Integer
  creature-ord (c) =
   when c
    is NoCreature -> 0
    is Elephant -> 1
    is Giraffe -> 2
    is Zebra -> 3
    is Rhino -> 4
    is DuckPond -> 5

  creatures : List Segment, Integer -> List Integer
  creatures (ss) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ss then []
    else [creature-ord (list-at ss i).exit-creature] & creatures ss (i + 1)

  exit-angles : List Segment, Integer -> List Real
  exit-angles (ss) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ss then []
    else [(list-at ss i).exit-angle] & exit-angles ss (i + 1)

  commits : List Segment, Integer -> List Real
  commits (ss) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ss then []
    else [(list-at ss i).commit-along] & commits ss (i + 1)

  headings : List Segment, Integer -> List Real
  headings (ss) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ss then []
    else [(list-at ss i).north-heading] & headings ss (i + 1)

Section: Every Tree, Cow and Pig

  trees-of : List Tree, Integer -> List Real
  trees-of (ts) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ts then []
    else let t = list-at ts i
    in [t.along, t.across, t.height] & trees-of ts (i + 1)

  all-trees : List Segment, Integer -> List Real
  all-trees (ss) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ss then []
    else (trees-of (list-at ss i).trees 0) & all-trees ss (i + 1)

  tree-colors-of : List Tree, Integer -> List Integer
  tree-colors-of (ts) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ts then []
    else [(list-at ts i).color] & tree-colors-of ts (i + 1)

  all-tree-colors : List Segment, Integer -> List Integer
  all-tree-colors (ss) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ss then []
    else (tree-colors-of (list-at ss i).trees 0) & all-tree-colors ss (i + 1)

  critters-of : List Critter, Integer -> List Real
  critters-of (cs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length cs then []
    else let c = list-at cs i
    in [c.along, c.across, c.height] & critters-of cs (i + 1)

  all-cows : List Segment, Integer -> List Real
  all-cows (ss) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ss then []
    else (critters-of (list-at ss i).cows 0) & all-cows ss (i + 1)

  cps-of : List Critter, Integer -> List Integer
  cps-of (cs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length cs then []
    else [(list-at cs i).codepoint] & cps-of cs (i + 1)

  all-cow-cps : List Segment, Integer -> List Integer
  all-cow-cps (ss) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ss then []
    else (cps-of (list-at ss i).cows 0) & all-cow-cps ss (i + 1)

  faces-of : List Critter, Integer -> List Boolean
  faces-of (cs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length cs then []
    else [(list-at cs i).face-right] & faces-of cs (i + 1)

  all-cow-faces : List Segment, Integer -> List Boolean
  all-cow-faces (ss) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ss then []
    else (faces-of (list-at ss i).cows 0) & all-cow-faces ss (i + 1)

  pigs-of : List Critter, Integer -> List Real
  pigs-of (cs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length cs then []
    else let c = list-at cs i
    in [c.along, c.across] & pigs-of cs (i + 1)

  all-pigs : List Segment, Integer -> List Real
  all-pigs (ss) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ss then []
    else (pigs-of (list-at ss i).pigs 0) & all-pigs ss (i + 1)

  gaze-pigs : List Segment, Integer -> List Real
  gaze-pigs (ss) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ss then []
    else let s = list-at ss i
    in let g = gaze-pig s.length (s.width / 2.0)
    in [g.along, g.across] & gaze-pigs ss (i + 1)

 The cat is read only where has-cat, which is the zig's own rule -- it leaves the
 field undefined otherwise.

  cats-of : List Segment, Integer -> List Real
  cats-of (ss) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ss then []
    else cat-or-skip ss i

  cat-or-skip : List Segment, Integer -> List Real
  cat-or-skip (ss) (i) =
    let s = list-at ss i
    in let rest = cats-of ss (i + 1)
    in if s.has-cat then [s.cat.along, s.cat.start-across, s.cat.mid-across, s.cat.end-across, s.cat.height] & rest else rest

Section: Distances

  route-dists : List Integer, Integer -> List Real
  route-dists (ns) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ns then []
    else [route-distance segs (list-at ns i) 137.5] & route-dists ns (i + 1)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "w-nsegs      " [list-length segs] g-w-nsegs)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "w-length     " (lengths segs 0) g-w-length 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "w-ntrees     " (n-trees segs 0) g-w-ntrees)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "w-ncows      " (n-cows segs 0) g-w-ncows)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "w-npigs      " (n-pigs segs 0) g-w-npigs)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "w-distract   " (distracts segs 0) g-w-distract)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "w-terminates " (terminates-of segs 0) g-w-terminates)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "w-hascat     " (has-cats segs 0) g-w-hascat)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "w-midtower   " (mid-towers segs 0) g-w-midtower)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "w-exitright  " (exit-rights segs 0) g-w-exitright)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "w-exitto     " (exit-tos segs 0) g-w-exitto)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "w-creature   " (creatures segs 0) g-w-creature)
    print-line-uni (grade-rel   "w-exitangle  " (exit-angles segs 0) g-w-exitangle 0.000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-rel   "w-commit     " (commits segs 0) g-w-commit 0.000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-rel   "w-heading    " (headings segs 0) g-w-heading 0.000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-rel   "w-trees      " (all-trees segs 0) g-w-trees 0.000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "w-treecolor  " (all-tree-colors segs 0) g-w-treecolor)
    print-line-uni (grade-rel   "w-cows       " (all-cows segs 0) g-w-cows 0.000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "w-cowcp      " (all-cow-cps segs 0) g-w-cowcp)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "w-cowface    " (all-cow-faces segs 0) g-w-cowface)
    print-line-uni (grade-rel   "w-pigs       " (all-pigs segs 0) g-w-pigs 0.000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-rel   "w-gazepig    " (gaze-pigs segs 0) g-w-gazepig 0.000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-rel   "w-cat        " (cats-of segs 0) g-w-cat 0.000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "w-course     " [course-length segs] g-w-course 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-rel   "w-routedist  " (route-dists [0, 1, 5, 12, 18] 0) g-w-routedist 0.000001)
  end
